From: Cider <cider@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d: Prefer copy-swap pixel formats for all swap effects.

swapchain_gl_present() falls back to swapchain_blit_gdi() whenever the pixel format's swap method is not
WGL_SWAP_COPY_ARB and the present covers only part of the client area. Letterboxed fullscreen games
(Kirikiri titles such as Senren*Banka on a 16:10 Mac display) hit this on every frame: glGetTexImage of the
whole back buffer, then a GDI StretchBlt into the window surface. Measured with scripts/wine-profile.py on an
M3 (macOS 26.7): the readback and GDI blit dominate the main thread at the title screen.

The Mac driver offers backing-store formats with copy semantics, so prefer them regardless of the
requested swap effect.

Cider-Topic: perf/wined3d
Upstream: candidate (wined3d pixel format scoring)
Cider-Test: Senren*Banka title screen, main thread CPU before/after

--- a/dlls/wined3d/context_gl.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/context_gl.c
@@ -1680,8 +1680,12 @@
             continue;
 
         value = 1;
-        if (swap_effect_copy && cfg->swap_method == WGL_SWAP_COPY_ARB)
-            value += 1;
+        /* Prefer copy-swap formats even for DISCARD/FLIP swapchains: without one, every present that does
+         * not cover the whole client area (e.g. a letterboxed fullscreen game) takes the GDI fallback in
+         * swapchain_gl_present(), a full GPU readback plus a GDI blit per frame. On macOS the Mac driver
+         * offers backing-store formats with copy semantics, which are far cheaper than that fallback. */
+        if (cfg->swap_method == WGL_SWAP_COPY_ARB)
+            value += swap_effect_copy ? 1 : 64;
         /* We try to locate a format which matches our requirements exactly. In case of
          * depth it is no problem to emulate 16-bit using e.g. 24-bit, so accept that. */
         if (cfg->depthSize == ds_format->depth_size)
